---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import BusinessPerspectiveNote from '../../components/BusinessPerspectiveNote.astro';
import ToolNextStep from '../../components/ToolNextStep.astro';
import StudentBusinessFeasibilityCalculator from '../../components/StudentBusinessFeasibilityCalculator.astro';
const title = 'Student Business Idea Feasibility Calculator';
const description = 'Check if a small student business idea can make money: break-even sales, profit per hour and a dated test plan with real buyers. Free and private.';
const canonical = 'https://futurecareerschool.com/tools/student-business-idea-feasibility-calculator/';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Nav /><BusinessPerspectiveNote /><main class="sbf-page"><div class="sbf-shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/career-resources/">Career resources</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><span aria-current="page">Student business idea feasibility calculator</span></nav>
    <p class="eyebrow">DECISION TOOL · USE YOUR OWN NUMBERS</p><h1>Test a student business idea before committing more</h1>
    <p class="lead">Type your guesses for price, cost, sales and hours. You see what you would keep each week, how many sales you need to break even, and a dated plan to test the idea with real buyers before you spend more.</p>
    <StudentBusinessFeasibilityCalculator />
    <section class="notes"><h2>What this calculator does not know</h2><p>It cannot know whether people will buy, whether your numbers are realistic, or whether the work fits your studies. It only shows the arithmetic of your guesses.</p>
    <h2>A worked example (an illustration, not a forecast)</h2><p>A student sells poster designs to local shops at ₹500 each. Each poster costs ₹50 to print, and the internet and tools cost ₹100 a week. That leaves ₹450 from each sale.</p><p>At 3 posters a week the student keeps ₹1,250 a week, which is about ₹208 for each of the 6 hours worked. One sale a week already covers the weekly cost, and 4 sales are needed to reach ₹1,500 a week.</p><p>The real question is whether 3 shops will pay every week, so the first test is to ask five shop owners.</p>
    <h2>When to talk to a person</h2><p>Tell a parent or teacher before you take money from customers. For food, home-made goods for sale or anything that needs a licence, ask the local authority or the official website of the rule maker first.</p>
    <p><a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/career-skills-compass/skills/">Build a skill you can demonstrate</a> · <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments/entrepreneurial-aptitude-test/">Try the entrepreneurial aptitude assessment</a> · <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/tools/education-cost-payback-planner/">Compare the education decision separately</a></p></section>
  </div>  <ToolNextStep toolName="Student Business Idea Feasibility Calculator" audience="student" />
  </main><Footer />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .sbf-page{min-height:70vh;padding:4rem 1.2rem;background:radial-gradient(circle at 20% 0%,rgba(229,184,74,.12),transparent 35%),#080c18}.sbf-shell{max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto}.breadcrumb{display:flex;gap:.55rem;flex-wrap:wrap;color:rgba(255,255,255,.55);font-size:.85rem;margin-bottom:2.5rem}.breadcrumb a,.notes a{color:#8de4d8;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px}.eyebrow{color:#e5b84a;font-size:.8rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em}.sbf-page h1{max-width:900px;font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,4rem);margin:.65rem 0 1rem;color:#fff;line-height:1.05}.lead{max-width:850px;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.7;color:rgba(255,255,255,.76)}.notes{margin-top:2rem;padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.15);border-radius:16px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.75);line-height:1.7}.notes h2{color:#fff}
</style>
